          },
          "confidence": 0.65,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-4c4b63775386b148",
          "evidence_type": "inquiry_or_scientific_method",
          "paraphrase": "The painter reflects on the dilemma of unbounded life on a finite planet.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [],
              "raw_id": "ev16",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "The painter pondered the mournful puzzle of life demanding to be born\nand, once born, demanding to be fruitful ... to multiply and to live as\nlong as possible--to do all that on a very small planet that would have\nto last forever."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 118,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00002"
            ],
            "start_char": 33
          },
          "confidence": 0.9,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-843d893516450c0d",
          "evidence_type": "storyworld_change",
          "paraphrase": "The society has eliminated prisons, poverty, disease, and war.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [],
              "raw_id": "ev01",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "There were no prisons, no slums, no insane asylums, no cripples, no\npoverty, no wars."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 9006,
            "paragraph_ids": [
              "p00069"
            ],
            "start_char": 8814
          },
          "confidence": 0.95,
          "entity_ids": [],
          "event_ids": [],
          "evidence_id": "sfev-875a994b0576ac76",
          "evidence_type": "extrapolative_consequence",
          "paraphrase": "Law requires a volunteer death for each newborn allowed to live.",
          "provenance": [
            {
              "backend": "anthropic",
              "normalization_notes": [],
              "raw_id": "ev08",
              "source": "model",
              "source_chunk_id": null
            }
          ],
          "quote": "The law said that no newborn child could survive unless the parents of\nthe child could find someone who would volunteer to die. Triplets, if\nthey were all to live, called for three volunteers."
        },
        {
          "anchor": {
            "end_char": 300,
